An efficient and clean way to solve this problem is to use a **Fenwick tree (Binary Indexed Tree)** with binary lifting.

Given the constraints that $num \le 10^5$, we can maintain:
1. A sliding window of the last $m$ elements using a circular array/queue.
2. A Fenwick tree for the **frequencies** of each number.
3. A Fenwick tree for the **sum of values** of each number.

To calculate the MK-Average:
- The sum of elements between the smallest $k$ and the smallest $m - k$ elements is simply:
  $$\text{sum}(\text{smallest } m - k) - \text{sum}(\text{smallest } k)$$
- We can find the sum of the smallest $r$ elements in $O(\log(\max(\text{num})))$ time using binary lifting directly on the Fenwick tree.
- The average is then this sum divided by $m - 2k$.

### Java 8 Implementation

```java
class MKAverage {
    private static final int MAX_VAL = 100000;
    private final int m;
    private final int k;
    private final int[] countTree;
    private final long[] sumTree;
    private final int[] stream;
    private int size;
    private int head;

    public MKAverage(int m, int k) {
        this.m = m;
        this.k = k;
        this.countTree = new int[MAX_VAL + 1];
        this.sumTree = new long[MAX_VAL + 1];
        this.stream = new int[m];
        this.size = 0;
        this.head = 0;
    }

    private void update(int val, int delta) {
        long deltaSum = (long) val * delta;
        for (int i = val; i <= MAX_VAL; i += i & -i) {
            countTree[i] += delta;
            sumTree[i] += deltaSum;
        }
    }

    private long getSumOfSmallest(int r) {
        if (r == 0) return 0;
        int idx = 0;
        int currentCount = 0;
        long currentSum = 0;

        for (int step = 1 << 16; step > 0; step >>= 1) {
            if (idx + step <= MAX_VAL && currentCount + countTree[idx + step] <= r) {
                idx += step;
                currentCount += countTree[idx];
                currentSum += sumTree[idx];
            }
        }

        if (currentCount < r) {
            currentSum += (long) (r - currentCount) * (idx + 1);
        }
        return currentSum;
    }

    public void addElement(int num) {
        if (size == m) {
            int oldNum = stream[head];
            update(oldNum, -1);
        } else {
            size++;
        }

        stream[head] = num;
        head = (head + 1) % m;
        update(num, 1);
    }

    public int calculateMKAverage() {
        if (size < m) {
            return -1;
        }
        long sumSmallestMK = getSumOfSmallest(m - k);
        long sumSmallestK = getSumOfSmallest(k);
        return (int) ((sumSmallestMK - sumSmallestK) / (m - 2 * k));
    }
}
```

