An elegant and optimal solution in Java for LeetCode's **"The Earliest and Latest Rounds Where Players Compete"**.

### Method Explanation

At each round, players at index $i$ and $n - i + 1$ (1-indexed) compete against each other.
1. If $p_1 + p_2 = n + 1$, `firstPlayer` and `secondPlayer` compete in the current round, so both the earliest and latest round from this state is `1`.
2. Otherwise, both players win their respective matches and advance to the next round with $m = \lfloor \frac{n + 1}{2} \rfloor$ players.
3. Every other match between $i$ and $n - i + 1$ can be decided in our favor. The winner will be placed at a position that determines the new 1-based positions $p_1'$ and $p_2'$ of `firstPlayer` and `secondPlayer`.
   Each pair $\{i, n - i + 1\}$ contributes to the number of winners before $p_1$ and $p_2$:
   - If both elements are $< p_1$, the winner is deterministically before both.
   - If both elements are between $p_1$ and $p_2$, the winner is deterministically between them.
   - If both elements are $> p_2$, the winner is deterministically after both.
   - If one element is $< p_1$ and the other is between $p_1$ and $p_2$, we can choose whether the winner is before $p_1$ or between them (Type A).
   - If one element is $< p_1$ and the other is $> p_2$, we can choose whether the winner is before $p_1$ or after $p_2$ (Type B).
   - If one element is between $p_1$ and $p_2$ and the other is $> p_2$, we can choose whether the winner is between them or after $p_2$ (Type C).

Since $n \le 28$, the number of such configurable pairs is very small ($c_A + c_B + c_C \le 12$). We can use memoized recursion (dynamic programming) over all valid next positions $(m, p_1', p_2')$ to find the minimum and maximum rounds.

### Java Source Code

```java
class Solution {
    private int[][][][] memo;

    public int[] earliestAndLatest(int n, int firstPlayer, int secondPlayer) {
        memo = new int[n + 1][n + 1][n + 1][2];
        return dfs(n, firstPlayer, secondPlayer);
    }

    private int[] dfs(int n, int p1, int p2) {
        if (p1 > p2) {
            int temp = p1;
            p1 = p2;
            p2 = temp;
        }

        // Base case: they play against each other
        if (p1 + p2 == n + 1) {
            return new int[]{1, 1};
        }

        if (memo[n][p1][p2][0] != 0) {
            return memo[n][p1][p2];
        }

        int m = (n + 1) / 2;
        int base1 = 0, base2 = 0;
        int cA = 0, cB = 0, cC = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i <= n / 2; i++) {
            int j = n - i + 1;

            if (i == p1 || j == p1) {
                // p1 wins, which is < p2 but not < p1
                base2++;
            } else if (i == p2 || j == p2) {
                // p2 wins, neither < p1 nor < p2
            } else {
                boolean iBeforeP1 = i < p1;
                boolean iBetween = i > p1 && i < p2;
                boolean jBetween = j > p1 && j < p2;
                boolean jAfterP2 = j > p2;

                if (iBeforeP1 && !jBetween && !jAfterP2) {
                    base1++;
                    base2++;
                } else if (!iBeforeP1 && iBetween && jBetween) {
                    base2++;
                } else if (!iBeforeP1 && !iBetween && jAfterP2) {
                    // Both after p2, contributes nothing
                } else if (iBeforeP1 && jBetween) {
                    cA++;
                } else if (iBeforeP1 && jAfterP2) {
                    cB++;
                } else if (iBetween && jAfterP2) {
                    cC++;
                }
            }
        }

        // Handle the middle player if n is odd
        if (n % 2 == 1) {
            int mid = (n + 1) / 2;
            if (mid < p1) {
                base1++;
                base2++;
            } else if (mid > p1 && mid < p2) {
                base2++;
            }
        }

        int minRound = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        int maxRound = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        // Iterate through all possible choices of winners
        for (int a = 0; a <= cA; a++) {
            for (int b = 0; b <= cB; b++) {
                for (int c = 0; c <= cC; c++) {
                    int nextP1 = 1 + base1 + a + b;
                    int nextP2 = 1 + base2 + cA + b + c;

                    int[] res = dfs(m, nextP1, nextP2);
                    minRound = Math.min(minRound, res[0] + 1);
                    maxRound = Math.max(maxRound, res[1] + 1);
                }
            }
        }

        memo[n][p1][p2] = new int[]{minRound, maxRound};
        return memo[n][p1][p2];
    }
}
